   "definition_quote": "We consider a multi-agent network with $N$ agents. ... Agents play the same $K$-armed bandit problem for $T$ time steps, send some values to their neighbors after each play ... We assume that rewards come from distributions that are subgaussian with variance proxy $\\sigma^2$. ... R(T) := TN\\mu_1 - \\E{\\sum_{t=1}^T \\sum_{i=1}^N \\mu_{I_{t,i}}} = \\sum_{k=1}^K \\Delta_k \\E{n_{T}^k}."
  },
